pedro and laura have been traveling  since may when they sold their business  and left their native cuba the pandemic  combined with u.s sanctions has caused  unprecedented food shortages and  hardship at home  last summer the communist regime in  havana faced its biggest protests in  decades leading to a harsh crackdown  the government talks about the external  embargo a great deal but there's an even  worse internal one the government seizes  agricultural production and distributes  food as it deems fit you cannot vote for  the president there are only certain  types of businesses you can be licensed  to do there's no democracy there are  people who disappear who've been killed  to get to greece laura and pedro flew to  moscow where cubans can travel without a  visa  from there they flew to belgrade also  visa-free then walked most of the way  through serbia and north macedonia into  greece  their goal was to reach spain or italy  they ended up on the greek island of  zakinthus where they planned to catch a  flight to milan in northern italy  but about 130 other cubans had the same  idea on the same day  this is what happened when police tried  to arrest them  it seems that this flight was oversold  and when the police saw one cuban  passport after another they put us all  into separate rooms they kept us there  for eight hours and told us they were  going to take us to a hotel instead they  took people to the police station their  woman children there pedro and laura  have now joined the thousands of  refugees who live legally or illegally  in athens  unlike african and asian nationals  who've sought asylum here for years  cubans in the balkans are a completely  new phenomenon greece is an attractive  way station for asylum seekers who want  to travel deeper into europe it has a  thousand kilometers of mountainous land  border which are difficult to police  and it's a member of the schengen area  which means that once here it's  relatively easy for someone to travel to  25 other european countries without  border controls  cuban's first port of call would  normally be the united states charles  cook is an immigration lawyer in the u.s  and explains what's happening the system  was broken by the trump administration  uh and so far the byte administration is  10 months in office has not really made  a lot of effort to fix that  because of coven so all these all these  factors are coming into play here that  are driving people to other places  and greece is the other place right now  hundreds of cubans are now in greece and  they're waiting to find out whether  authorities will take up their asylum  applications or encourage them to keep  walking  john saropolos al jazeera athens
 

